```
D02 One IP signs in to O365 as several different users (T1078.004)
An attacker holding several stolen passwords often uses them all from the same server.
first_alert is when the second account signs in, which is when this would fire as a
scheduled search over the last 24 hours. Excludes Microsoft's own addresses. A shared office
or VPN egress IP will also match: list known egress IPs in the NOT clause once you have a baseline.
```
index=botsv3 sourcetype=ms:o365:management Operation=UserLoggedIn
| where NOT cidrmatch("40.0.0.0/8", ClientIP) AND NOT cidrmatch("52.96.0.0/12", ClientIP)
| stats min(_time) as account_first_login by ClientIP UserId
| sort 0 ClientIP account_first_login
| streamstats count as nth values(UserId) as accounts by ClientIP
| where nth = 2
| eval first_alert=strftime(account_first_login, "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S")
| table first_alert ClientIP accounts
